=== A. is a band generic across constructions? ===
construction                          exact  resolved       band  width
168: t=3x+97, A=t*t, B=t>>2              20        16    [16,19]      4
A=t*t, t=x+97 (smaller node)             17        16    [16,16]      1
A=t*3 (linear branch)                    12        10    [10,11]      2
A=t*t*t (cubic branch)                   30        24    [24,29]      6
A=t>>1 (contracting branch)               9         7      [7,8]      2
t=x (identity node), A=t*t               16        16      empty      0

C3 some construction has an empty band : True   (want True)

=== B. is branch B's loss measured across the band, or at one width? ===
    168's construction: exact needs 20 bits, resolved needs 16, band [16, 17, 18, 19]
 carrier  in band  inputs worse  total extra |err|
      14    False           203              15504
      15    False           203              15504
      16     True           203              15504
      17     True           203              15504
      18     True           203              15504
      19     True           203              15504
      20    False           203              15504
      21    False           203              15504
      22    False           203              15504

C1 loss is independent of the carrier width : confirmed below
C2 width 16 reproduces 168's 203 / 15504     : True   (got (203, 15504))

VERDICT
  Branch B's loss is IDENTICAL at every carrier width swept:
    1 distinct (worse, total) pair(s) across 9 widths -> {(203, 15504)}
  which is what the model forces: B's loss depends on whether t is
  resolved, and nothing in B's computation reads the carrier at all.

  So the band is not a measured boundary. It is the interval
  [resolved_need, exact_need - 1], entailed by p6's own inequality, and
  the ONE thing measured in it is the loss at a single width, which is
  the same number at every other width. The claim 'the conflict exists
  at 16 through 19' is arithmetic on two observed widths plus one
  measurement that does not vary across them.

  That does NOT make it an artifact of the construction. The sweep above
  shows a band appears whenever the exact form needs more than the
  resolved one, which is generic, and vanishes exactly when they agree.
  The bound is right. What is wrong is calling it measured.
